{"c": 32, "r": 64, "b": ""}}, {"name": "Eastern Towhee", "sci": "Pipilo erythrophthalmus", "n": 4, "first": "9:48 AM", "last": "9:49 AM", "ts": 1793195291, "mins": [588, 588, 588, 589], "anim": null, "trunk": false, "fact": "Towhees scratch through leaf litter with a two-footed hop-and-kick. The song says it all: “drink-your-teeeea.”", "vox": "sounds/voice/pipilo-erythrophthalmus.mp3?v=1793113027", "snd": "sounds/pipilo-erythrophthalmus.mp3?v=1793113162", "sndby": "Ross Gallardy, xeno-canto XC310201, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0", "life": true, "key": "towhee", "cm": 20.0, "img": "cutouts/towhee.png", "w": 800, "h": 545, "len": 636.0, "beak": [0.64, 0.09, "R"], "mask": {"c": 32, "r": 22, "b": "AAHwAAAD+AAAB/gAAA/wAAAf8AAAP/ADAH/wBgD/8BwB/+B4Af/g8AP/wcAD/8cAA/8eAAf/+AAfE+AAHh+AAD4fgAB8fAAA+PwAAPPAAAAPAAAADgAAAA=="}}, {"name": "Pileated Woodpecker", "sci": "Dryocopus pileatus", "n": 3, "first": "9:57 AM", "last": "10:04 AM", "ts": 1793195870, "mins": [597, 603, 604], "anim": null, "trunk": false, "fact": "It chisels big rectangular holes in dead wood while hunting carpenter ants. Abandoned holes later shelter owls, ducks and other cavity nesters.", "vox": "sounds/voice/dryocopus-pileatus.mp3?v=1793112997", "snd": "sounds/dryocopus-pileatus.mp3?v=1793113171", "sndby": "Mike Nelson, xeno-canto XC102028, CC BY-NC-ND 2.5", "key": "pileated", "cm": 45.0, "img": "cutouts/pileated.png", "w": 649, "h": 800, "len": 737.0, "beak": [0.42, 0.1, "R"], "mask": {"c": 32, "r": 39, "b": "AAAf/gAAH/4AAB/+Bzwf/x/4H/9/8B///+Af/3/AH/8/8B//D/wf/wf+H/8D/x//Af+f/wP/n/8D/5//A////wH///8B////Af///wH///4A/9/+AP/f/gD/3/4Af5//AH+f/wA/v/4AP7//AB+//wAf//8AD///AAf//wAH//8ABv/+AAD//gAAf/4AAH//AAA//wAAP/8AAD/+"}}, {"name": "American Crow", "sci": "Corvus brachyrhynchos", "n": 24, "first": "10:52 AM", "last": "12:48 PM", "ts": 1793199155, "mins": [652, 652, 655, 682, 683, 684, 685, 685, 689, 694, 696, 696, 713, 715, 716, 716, 716, 717, 719, 719, 719, 745, 767, 768], "anim": null, "trunk": false, "fact": "Crows remember individual human faces for years, and they seem to pass the grudge along to other crows.", "vox": "sounds/voice/corvus-brachyrhynchos.mp3?v=1793112990", "snd": "sounds/corvus-brachyrhynchos.mp3?v=1793113335", "sndby": "David Vander Pluym, xeno-canto XC289011, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0", "key": "crow", "cm": 45.0, "img": "cutouts/crow.png", "w": 553, "h": 364, "len": 568.0, "beak": [0.94, 0.14, "R"], "mask": {"c": 32, "r": 21, "b": "AAAHwAAAD/gAAB/+AAB//gAD/+AAD//AAB//wAB//4AB//+AB///AAf//wAP//4AH//4AH//8AD//8AA/x+AAPgPwAbwF/6/f////3///7Bhw5AA"}}, {"name": "Hairy Woodpecker", "sci": "Leuconotopicus villosus", "n": 3, "first": "11:06 AM", "last": "11:09 AM", "ts": 1793199970, "mins": [666, 667, 669], "anim": null, "trunk": false, "vox": "sounds/voice/leuconotopicus-villosus.mp3?v=1793200104", "snd": "sounds/leuconotopicus-villosus.mp3?v=1793200052", "sndby": "Frank Lambert, xeno-canto XC408592, CC BY-NC-ND 4.0", "life": true, "key": "ph-hairywoodpecker", "ph": true, "cm": 15, "img": "", "w": 560, "h": 440, "len": 470}, {"name": "Golden-crowned Kinglet", "sci": "Regulus satrapa", "n": 3, "first": "11:25 AM", "last": "11:26 AM", "ts": 1793201117, "mins": [685, 685, 686], "anim": null, "trunk": false, "fact": "One of the tiniest songbirds here, yet it survives freezing winter nights by shivering, puffing up its feathers, and huddling with others.", "vox": "sounds/voice/regulus-satrapa.mp3?v=1793113033", "snd": "sounds/regulus-satrapa.mp3?v=1793113145", "sndby": "Mike Nelson, xeno-canto XC135597, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0", "key": "goldenkinglet", "cm": 10.0, "img": "cutouts/goldenkinglet.png", "w": 800, "h": 541, "len": 578.0, "beak": [0.9, 0.13, "R"], "mask": {"c": 32, "r": 22, "b": "AAAH4AAAH+DAAH/44AD/8HgD/+AeB//gDw//wAO//8AB///AAf//gAH//wAAh/wAAAPwAAAA+AAAAD4AAAAPAAAAD8AAAAHwAAAAeAAAAB4AAAAPAAAABw=="}}, {"name": "Downy Woodpecker", "sci": "Dryobates pubescens", "n": 3, "first": "11:54 AM", "last": "1:13 PM", "ts": 1793202896, "mins": [714, 715, 793], "anim": null, "trunk": false, "f